      "anchor": {
        "mission_intent": "Subject: Full RMF Alignment Specification for Financial Reporting Systems \u2014 Authorization Streamlining Initiative\n\nTeam, as we prepare for the upcoming audit cycle, I need a comprehensive specification document that aligns our financial reporting information systems with the NIST SP 800-37 Rev. 2 Risk Management Framework, specifically addressing the Prepare step at both the organization and system levels. The spec should establish a consistent baseline starting point for RMF execution across all financial reporting platforms, including our General Ledger (SAP FICO), the consolidation engine (OneStream), and the SEC filing portal interface. We need to maximize the use of common controls to ensure standardized, cost-effective security and privacy inheritance across these systems, and the document must identify where shared or cloud-based services can reduce the total number of authorization packages we maintain. Include organizationally-tailored control baselines that accelerate security and privacy plan development while promoting consistency of plan content. For each delegated task, clearly map the accountable role that retains primary responsibility for completion even when execution is delegated downstream. The specification should reference applicable control families, define the authorization boundaries for each system, and ensure all outputs from the Prepare step are documented so we can present a defensible posture to our external auditors. Please have the draft ready for leadership review by end of next quarter.",
